{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the §7 toml/nginx port coupling explicit (state `http_port = 8000` in the toml block or note the nginx `:8000` target tracks `http_port`).","criteria":["maintainability","edge-cases"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["New §7 toml sets `http_host = \"127.0.0.1\"` and `http_path = \"/mcp\"` but no `http_port`","New §7 nginx block: `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp;` (port 8000 hardcoded)","§1 (docs/mcp-auth.md:23) documents `http_port = 8000` as the default the recipe implicitly depends on"],"finding":"The §7 `[tool.rebar.mcp]` config block sets `http_host` but omits `http_port`, while the accompanying nginx block hardcodes `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000...`. The recipe silently relies on the default port (8000, documented only in §1) being unchanged; a reader who sets a different `http_port` will have an nginx target that no longer matches, with nothing in §7 flagging the coupling.","id":"1","impact":0.3,"location":"docs/mcp-auth.md (new §7 toml + nginx blocks)","norm_id":"n096ab152b0c8ddd4","priority":0.2571,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"low","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}}],"blocking":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify the §7 nginx `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp;` under `location /mcp/` actually maps edge `/mcp/<suffix>` to app `/mcp/<suffix>` (nginx prefix-replacement drops the slash and concatenates the suffix); align with the URI-less §5 pattern or use a matching trailing-slash proxy_pass.","criteria":["correctness","maintainability"],"decision":"block","evidence":["New §7: `location /mcp/ {` with `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp;` and comment `# external https://<box>/mcp/  →  loopback app http_path /mcp`","§5 reference recipe (docs/mcp-auth.md:200-201): `location /mcp {` / `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;` (URI-less, preserves full path)","nginx semantics: a proxy_pass with a URI replaces the location-matched prefix, so `location /mcp/` + `proxy_pass .../mcp` yields `/mcp` for `/mcp/` and `/mcp<suffix>` for `/mcp/<suffix>`"],"finding":"The new §7 nginx recipe uses `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp;` under `location /mcp/`. Because this proxy_pass carries a URI, nginx replaces the matched `/mcp/` prefix with `/mcp`, so `/mcp/` proxies to `/mcp` (trailing slash dropped) and any subpath `/mcp/<x>` proxies to `/mcp<x>` (e.g. `/mcp/messages` -> `/mcpmessages`), not `/mcp/messages`. The §5 reference recipe deliberately uses a URI-less `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;` which preserves the full request path. The §7 comment claiming the edge maps `/mcp/` -> app `/mcp` is misleading and the recipe likely mis-routes subpaths.","id":"0","impact":0.6,"location":"docs/mcp-auth.md (new §7 nginx block)","norm_id":"naa048c77dfa151fb","priority":0.6,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":[],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Match the §5 pattern: either use `location /mcp/ { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp/; }` (both trailing slashes, so `/mcp/<x>` -> `/mcp/<x>`) or a URI-less `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;` with the app path aligned; and correct the mapping comment accordingly.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"local","capability_degraded":true,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":false,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":true,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"sometimes","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}}],"change_fingerprin